===== J2-65-R18-SaturationSchur.py =====
SATURATION_BEFORE_SCHUR:
pre-Schur cyclotomic row saturation is trivial: C_cyc=0
Schur then lands in the q-free order with second norm coordinate V=q^2*v0
SCHUR_BEFORE_SATURATION:
Schur first gives Z[q^2*sqrt(D0)] inside Z[sqrt(D0)]
post-Schur q-free order saturation enlarges exactly the sqrt-coordinate by index q^2
SATURATION_SCHUR_COMMUTATION=FINITE_INDEX
COMMUTATION_DEFECT_MODULE=Z/q^2Z
COMMUTATION_DEFECT_ORDER=q^2
INDEX_CONDUCTOR_CORRESPONDENCE=PROVED_FOR_THE_UNIVERSAL_q_PART
INTERPRETATION=the R17 order index and the universal source norm-coordinate q-packet are the same cokernel
RETURN_CODE=0

===== J2-65-R18-SourcePacket.py =====
SOURCE_PACKET_CYCLOTOMIC_ROW_REDUCTION=PASS
u^5*q^4*(q+4) == 1+4u (mod G)
u^5*(q+2)^3*(q+4) == u*(1+2u)^3*(1+4u) (mod G)
PRE_SCHUR_Q_FREE_CONGRUENCE:
G | 2*d*(1+4*u)*(Z+u*(1+2*u)^3*a)
delta0=gcd(G,2*d*(1+4*u)); M0=G/delta0
q_INDEPENDENT_BASE_COORDINATE_RETIRED=TRUE
RETURN_CODE=0

